B.ZU=new A.bw("Although the novelist's early works were dismissed by critics as overly sentimental, her later novels, with their spare prose and unflinching portraits of rural poverty, earned her a reputation for ______ that few of her contemporaries could match.",u.Y,B.Rr,'"spare prose" (ortiqchasiz uslub) va "unflinching" (hissiyotga berilmay) \u2014 yozuvchi o\'zini tutib yozadi \u2192 restraint (vazminlik). "Although" erta asarlardagi "sentimental" uslubga qarama-qarshilikni ko\'rsatadi.')
B.QH=s(["irreversible","observable","unprecedented","gradual"],t.s)
B.a_0=new A.bw("Marine biologists warn that the decline of many coral reefs is serious, but they insist it is not ______: with sharp cuts in emissions and strong local protection, many reefs could recover within a few decades.",u.Y,B.QH,'Gapning davomi: "could recover" \u2014 tiklanishi mumkin. Demak, jarayon qaytarib bo\'lmaydigan (irreversible) emas.')
B.Se=s(["ignores","corrects","extends","praises"],t.s)
B.a_8=new A.bw("Critics of historian Karim Nazarov claim that he ______ earlier scholarship on medieval trade, but in fact his study builds directly on those findings, even as it corrects several of their assumptions.",u.Y,B.Se,'"but in fact ... builds directly on those findings" \u2014 tanqidchilarning fikri bunga zid bo\'lishi kerak: u avvalgi ishlarni e\'tiborsiz qoldiradi (ignores). "corrects" va "extends" \u2014 u haqiqatan ham shunday qiladi, zidlik yo\'q.')
B.R_=s(["efficient","ornate","fragile","controversial"],t.s)
B.a_u=new A.bw("The new bridge design is remarkably ______: engineers assembled its prefabricated sections in just eleven days, a fraction of the time required for a conventional bridge of similar size.",u.Y,B.R_,"Ikki nuqtadan keyingi tushuntirish \u2014 juda tez qurildi \u2192 efficient (samarali).")
B.R7=s(["arbitrary","vivid","traditional","precise"],t.s)
B.a_4=new A.bw("Some readers find the poet's imagery ______, but careful study reveals that each seemingly random image is connected to the collection's central theme of migration.",u.Y,B.R7,"\"seemingly random\" (tasodifiy ko'rinadigan) \u2192 arbitrary (o'zboshimchalik bilan tanlangan, tartibsiz).")
B.SA=s(["inconclusive","definitive","fabricated","predictable"],t.s)
B.a_c=new A.bw("Because the results of the first trial were ______, the research team designed a second experiment with a much larger sample to determine whether the treatment truly had an effect.",u.Y,B.SA,"Ikkinchi tajriba \"haqiqatan ta'siri bormi\" \u2014 aniqlash uchun kerak bo'ldi. Demak, birinchi natija aniq xulosa bermagan \u2192 inconclusive.")
B.T_=s(["restrained in speech and manner","booked in advance","kept for later use","doubtful"],t.s)
B.ZZ=new A.bw('The new student was reserved during her first week, answering questions politely but rarely offering her own opinions.\n\nAs used in the text, what does the word "reserved" most nearly mean?',"Choose the best meaning.",B.T_,"Kontekst: savollarga muloyim javob beradi, lekin o'z fikrini kam aytadi \u2192 o'zini tutadigan, kamgap. \"booked in advance\" \u2014 so'zning boshqa (bron qilingan) ma'nosi, bu yerga mos emas.")
B.SY=s(["reliable","loud","healthy","deep"],t.s)
B.ZN=new A.bw('After reviewing data from three independent laboratories, the committee concluded that the study\'s methods were sound and that its conclusions could be trusted.\n\nAs used in the text, what does the word "sound" most nearly mean?',"Choose the best meaning.",B.SY,'"conclusions could be trusted" \u2014 usullar ishonchli \u2192 reliable. "sound" ning eng mashhur ma\'nosi (tovush) bu yerda emas.')
B.NC=s([B.ZU,B.a_0,B.a_8,B.a_u,B.a_4,B.a_c,B.ZZ,B.ZN],t.vn)
B.a_A=new A.ed("wic","Words in Context","So'zning matndagi ma'nosi","\ud83d\udd24","Craft and Structure","Variantlarga qaramasdan oldin bo'sh joyga o'zingiz mos so'z o'ylang (o'zbekcha bo'lsa ham). Matndagi kalit so'zlarga e'tibor bering: 'although', 'but', 'not' \u2014 qarama-qarshilikni, ':' va 'because' \u2014 tushuntirishni bildiradi. So'zning eng mashhur ma'nosiga aldanmang.",B.NC)
B.SG=s(["Specifically","However","Nevertheless","In contrast"],t.s)
B.a__=new A.bw("Honeybees can learn to recognize individual human faces in laboratory experiments. ______, the insects learn to associate a particular face with a sugar reward and then return to that face again and again.",u.J,B.SG,"Ikkinchi gap birinchisini aniqlashtiradi \u2014 qanday qilib tanishini tushuntiradi \u2192 Specifically.")
B.RD=s(["As a result","For instance","Even so","Similarly"],t.s)
B.a_p=new A.bw("Early telescopes produced blurry images because their lenses bent different colors of light by different amounts. ______, seventeenth-century astronomers often struggled to see fine details on the surfaces of planets.",u.J,B.RD,"Xira tasvir \u2014 sabab, detallarni ko'ra olmaslik \u2014 natija \u2192 As a result.")
B.PY=s(["In fact","Therefore","Likewise","Finally"],t.s)
B.ZM=new A.bw("Many people assume that deserts are nearly lifeless. ______, the Kyzylkum Desert supports hundreds of species of plants, reptiles, and birds adapted to its extreme temperatures.",u.J,B.PY,"Ikkinchi gap keng tarqalgan fikrni rad etadi \u2192 In fact (aslida esa).")
B.Tk=s(["Subsequently","Conversely","For example","Nonetheless"],t.s)
B.a_k=new A.bw("The architect's first design was rejected because it was too expensive. ______, she submitted a revised plan that used locally produced brick and reduced costs by 30 percent.",u.J,B.Tk,"Voqealar ketma-ketligi: avval rad etildi, keyin yangi reja \u2192 Subsequently (keyinroq).")
B.Pu=s(["However","Thus","In addition","For this reason"],t.s)
B.a_9=new A.bw("Solar panels produce no emissions while they operate. ______, manufacturing them requires energy and raw materials, so their environmental impact is not zero.",u.J,B.Pu,"Birinchi gap afzallik, ikkinchisi cheklov \u2192 zidlik: However.")
B.Py=s(["Moreover","Instead","In contrast","Regardless"],t.s)
B.a_f=new A.bw("The study found that students who slept at least eight hours performed better on memory tests. ______, these students were also more likely to report feeling calm before exams.",u.J,B.Py,"Ikkinchi gap yana bir ijobiy natijani qo'shadi \u2192 Moreover (bundan tashqari).")
B.Td=s(["by contrast","for example","therefore","similarly"],t.s)
B.a_d=new A.bw("Some languages, such as English, rely heavily on word order to show who did what to whom. Other languages, ______, use word endings to mark grammatical roles, allowing words to appear in many different orders.",u.J,B.Td,"Ikki xil tillar taqqoslanmoqda va ular bir-biriga qarama-qarshi \u2192 by contrast.")
B.On=s([B.a__,B.a_p,B.ZM,B.a_k,B.a_9,B.a_f,B.a_d],t.vn)
B.a_C=new A.ed("transitions","Transitions","Bog'lovchi so'zlar","\ud83d\udd17","Expression of Ideas","Ikki gap orasidagi mantiqiy aloqani aniqlang:\n\u2022 zidlik \u2014 however, nevertheless, in contrast, by contrast\n\u2022 natija \u2014 therefore, as a result, thus, consequently\n\u2022 qo'shimcha \u2014 moreover, in addition, furthermore\n\u2022 aniqlashtirish / misol \u2014 specifically, for example, in fact\n\u2022 vaqt tartibi \u2014 subsequently, then, finally",B.On)
B.TJ=s(["world;","world,","world","world and"],t.s)
B.a_h=new A.bw("The Aral Sea was once the fourth-largest lake in the ______ by the early 2000s, however, it had lost most of its water.",u.Q,B.TJ,"Ikkala qism ham to'liq gap. Ularni vergulsiz yoki faqat vergul bilan ulash xato \u2192 nuqtali vergul (;).")
B.QO=s(["artifacts:","artifacts;","artifacts, and","artifacts. A"],t.s)
B.a_b=new A.bw("The museum's newest exhibit features three rare ______ a bronze mirror, a silk banner, and a painted ceramic bowl.",u.Q,B.QO,"Oldin to'liq gap, keyin ro'yxat \u2192 ikki nuqta (:). Nuqtali vergul va nuqtadan keyin to'liq gap kelishi kerak edi.")
B.R2=s(["Warsaw,","Warsaw;","Warsaw","Warsaw:"],t.s)
B.a_n=new A.bw("Marie Curie, who was born in ______ became the first person to win Nobel Prizes in two different sciences.",u.Q,B.R2,'"who was born in Warsaw" \u2014 qo\'shimcha izoh. U vergul bilan boshlangan, demak vergul bilan yopilishi kerak.')
B.Nw=s(["cold, and","cold,","cold","cold and,"],t.s)
B.ZY=new A.bw("The engineers tested the new battery in extreme ______ it continued to work at temperatures as low as minus forty degrees Celsius.",u.Q,B.Nw,"Ikki to'liq gap \u2192 vergul + and. Faqat vergul (comma splice) xato.")
B.QG=s(["nutcrackers","nutcrackers,","nutcrackers;","nutcrackers:"],t.s)
B.a_o=new A.bw("Researchers studying ______ found that these birds can remember the locations of thousands of hidden seeds for months.",u.Q,B.QG,'"Researchers studying nutcrackers" \u2014 gapning egasi, "found" \u2014 kesim. Ega va kesim orasida tinish belgisi bo\'lmaydi.')
B.OS=s(["world; in fact,","world, in fact,","world in fact","world, in fact"],t.s)
B.ZV=new A.bw("The festival attracts visitors from around the ______ many of them return year after year.",u.Q,B.OS,'Ikki to\'liq gap; "in fact" ikkinchi gapga tegishli \u2192 world; in fact,')
B.Qw=s([B.a_h,B.a_b,B.a_n,B.ZY,B.a_o,B.ZV],t.vn)
B.a_x=new A.ed("boundaries","Boundaries","Tinish belgilari","\u2702\ufe0f","Standard English Conventions","Avval to'liq (mustaqil) gaplarni toping.\n\u2022 Ikki to'liq gapni FAQAT vergul bilan ulab bo'lmaydi: nuqta, nuqtali vergul (;) yoki \", and / , but\" kerak.\n\u2022 Ikki nuqta (:) dan oldin to'liq gap, keyin \u2014 tushuntirish yoki ro'yxat.\n\u2022 Ega bilan kesim orasiga vergul qo'yilmaydi.\n\u2022 Qo'shimcha izoh (who..., which...) ikki tomondan vergul bilan ajratiladi.",B.Qw)
B.l5=s(["is","are","were","have been"],t.s)
B.ZW=new A.bw("The collection of letters written by the explorer during his travels ______ now housed in the national library.",u.Q,B.l5,'Ega \u2014 "collection" (birlik). "letters" \u2014 faqat izoh qismi \u2192 is.')
B.a_e=new A.bw("Each of the students in the robotics club ______ responsible for designing one part of the machine.",u.Q,B.l5,'"Each" \u2014 birlik \u2192 is.')
B.OF=s(["darkened","darkens","will darken","has darkened"],t.s)
B.a_t=new A.bw('When Mount Tambora erupted in 1815, ash and gases ______ the sky for months, contributing to what became known as "the year without a summer" in 1816.',u.Q,B.OF,"O'tgan zamondagi voqea (1815, erupted) \u2192 Past Simple: darkened.")
B.Rz=s(["had repeated","repeat","will repeat","are repeating"],t.s)
B.ZT=new A.bw("The scientists published their findings only after they ______ the experiment three times.",u.Q,B.Rz,"Tajriba nashrdan OLDIN takrorlangan \u2192 Past Perfect: had repeated.")
B.S8=s(["were","was","is","has been"],t.s)
B.ZS=new A.bw("Neither the director nor the actors ______ aware that the camera was still recording.",u.Q,B.S8,"neither... nor... da kesim yaqinroq egaga (the actors \u2014 ko'plik) moslanadi \u2192 were.")
B.Rg=s(["Dilnoza finished the marathon in under four hours.","the marathon was finished by Dilnoza in under four hours.","Dilnoza's marathon time was under four hours.","the four-hour mark was beaten by Dilnoza."],t.s)
B.ZX=new A.bw("Having trained for months, ______",u.Q,B.Rg,'Oylab mashq qilgan \u2014 Dilnoza. Shuning uchun verguldan keyin darhol "Dilnoza" kelishi kerak.')
B.a_a=new A.bw("The giant panda's diet consists almost entirely of bamboo, a plant that ______ low in nutrients, so pandas must eat for many hours each day.",u.Q,B.l5,'"a plant that ..." \u2014 that birlik "plant" ga ishora qiladi va hozirgi fakt \u2192 is.')
