B.a_y=new A.ed("form","Form, Structure, and Sense","Grammatik moslik","\ud83e\udde9","Standard English Conventions","\u2022 Egani toping va orasidagi so'zlarga aldanmang: \"The collection of letters IS...\"\n\u2022 each, every, neither (yolg'iz) \u2014 birlik.  neither... nor... \u2014 kesim yaqinroq egaga moslanadi.\n\u2022 Zamonlar mantiqan mos bo'lsin: o'tmishdagi ikki voqeadan oldingisi \u2014 had + V3.\n\u2022 Gap boshidagi \"-ing\" qismi aynan shu ishni qilgan kishiga tegishli bo'lishi kerak.",B.PT)
B.TO=s(["Bukhara's position on trade routes helped make it a major center of learning as well as commerce.","Silk and spices were the most valuable goods traded in Bukhara.","Scholars in Bukhara focused mainly on astronomy rather than medicine.","Merchants in Bukhara were more interested in religion than in trade."],t.s)
B.a_5=new A.bw("For centuries, the city of Bukhara sat at the crossroads of trade routes linking China, Persia, and Europe. Merchants arriving in its markets brought not only silk and spices but also new ideas, religions, and technologies. Scholars from distant regions gathered in its madrasas, exchanging knowledge in mathematics, medicine, and astronomy. As a result, Bukhara became more than a commercial hub; it developed into one of the most important intellectual centers of the medieval Islamic world.",u.h,B.TO,"Oxirgi gap xulosa: Buxoro savdo markazidan ilm markaziga aylandi. Boshqa variantlar \u2014 tor detal yoki matnda yo'q fikr.")
B.Ra=s(["Each arm can react to its surroundings somewhat independently.","Octopuses have larger central brains than most animals.","Octopuses cannot taste food with their arms.","Octopuses must use their central brain to grasp food."],t.s)
B.ZR=new A.bw("An octopus has roughly 500 million neurons, but about two-thirds of them are located in its arms rather than in its central brain. This unusual arrangement allows each arm to respond to touch and taste largely on its own. In experiments, an arm can reach toward food and grasp it without direct instructions from the brain. Researchers believe this distributed system helps octopuses carry out many complex tasks at once.","According to the text, what is one result of the way octopus neurons are distributed?",B.Ra,'Matnda: "allows each arm to respond ... largely on its own" \u2014 har bir qo\'l ancha mustaqil harakat qiladi.')
B.T6=s(["A memory helps a nervous character begin her performance.","A character decides to stop playing the piano.","A grandmother teaches a character a new melody.","Judges criticize a character's choice of music."],t.s)
B.a_1=new A.bw("The following text is from a short story.\n\nNodira had practiced the piano piece for weeks, yet when she sat down in front of the judges, her hands felt like someone else's. She stared at the keys. Then she remembered her grandmother's small kitchen, where she had first played the melody on an old, out-of-tune piano while her grandmother hummed along. Nodira took a breath, and her fingers began to move.","Which choice best describes what happens in the text?",B.T6,"Nodira hayajonlanadi, buvisining oshxonasini eslaydi va chalishni boshlaydi \u2192 xotira unga yordam berdi.")
B.Sy=s(["A popular belief about the Great Wall's visibility from space is not accurate.","The Great Wall is the longest structure ever built by humans.","Astronauts can easily see the Great Wall from low Earth orbit.","The Great Wall was built using materials brought from far away."],t.s)
B.a_g=new A.bw("Many people believe that the Great Wall of China can be seen from the Moon with the naked eye. However, astronauts who have traveled to the Moon report that no human-made structures are visible from that distance. Even from low Earth orbit, the wall is extremely difficult to spot, because it is narrow and built from materials similar in color to the surrounding land.",u.h,B.Sy,"Matn keng tarqalgan fikrni (Oydan ko'rinadi) dalillar bilan rad etadi.")
B.Pe=s([B.a_5,B.ZR,B.a_1,B.a_g],t.vn)
B.a_z=new A.ed("central","Central Ideas and Details","Asosiy g'oya va tafsilotlar","\ud83c\udfaf","Information and Ideas","Matnni o'qib, uni bitta gap bilan o'zingiz xulosa qiling, keyin variantlarni taqqoslang.\nXato variantlar odatda: juda tor (bitta detal), juda keng yoki matnda umuman aytilmagan fikr.",B.Pe)
B.TN=s(["a higher number of eggs does not necessarily lead to a larger adult frog population.","the frogs lay fewer eggs when streams are moving quickly.","heavy rainfall has no effect on the frogs' reproduction.","tadpoles survive better in fast-moving streams than in calm water."],t.s)
B.a_7=new A.bw("Researchers found that a species of frog in Panama lays more eggs in years with heavy rainfall. However, in those same years, fewer tadpoles survive to adulthood, because fast-moving streams wash many of them away. These findings suggest that ______",u.p,B.TN,"Tuxum ko'p, lekin kam itbaliq omon qoladi \u2192 ko'p tuxum hali katta populyatsiya degani emas.")
B.SK=s(["reading for pleasure causes teenagers' vocabulary to improve.","some teenagers read printed books for pleasure.","homes differ in the number of books they contain.","vocabulary test scores varied among the teenagers."],t.s)
B.ZO=new A.bw("In a survey of 2,000 teenagers, those who read printed books for pleasure at least three times a week scored higher on vocabulary tests than those who did not. However, the teenagers who read more also tended to come from homes with more books. Therefore, the survey alone cannot show that ______",u.p,B.SK,"Boshqa omil (uydagi kitoblar) ham bor, shuning uchun so'rovnoma SABAB-NATIJANI isbotlay olmaydi. Qolgan variantlar so'rovnomada aniq ko'rsatilgan.")
B.S4=s(["the region's landscape or the settlers' trade networks were likely different in the past.","the settlers never ate fish.","the fishhooks were made only recently.","the settlement was built on a seashore that still exists today."],t.s)
B.a_v=new A.bw("Archaeologists excavating an ancient settlement found fish bones and fishhooks carved from bone, even though the site is now more than 200 kilometers from the nearest sea or large lake. The archaeologists concluded that ______",u.p,B.S4,"Baliq qoldiqlari bor, lekin hozir suv uzoq \u2192 o'tmishda geografiya yoki savdo aloqalari boshqacha bo'lgan. Ehtiyotkor xulosa (\"likely\") \u2014 SAT uchun yaxshi belgi.")
B.Nx=s(["gives the plants enough time to produce seeds before the cold returns.","prevents the plants from being pollinated.","shows that Arctic plants do not need sunlight.","means that Arctic plants live longer than other plants."],t.s)
B.a_2=new A.bw("Some plants in the Arctic flower within days after the snow melts, while similar species in warmer regions take several weeks to flower. Because the Arctic summer is very short, this rapid flowering most likely ______",u.p,B.Nx,"Yoz qisqa \u2192 tez gullash urug' berishga ulgurish uchun kerak.")
B.PJ=s([B.a_7,B.ZO,B.a_v,B.a_2],t.vn)
B.a_B=new A.ed("inferences","Inferences","Mantiqiy xulosa","\ud83e\udde0","Information and Ideas","Matndagi dalillardan BEVOSITA kelib chiqadigan xulosani tanlang. Juda kuchli da'volar (always, never, proves) va matnda asosi yo'q taxminlardan ehtiyot bo'ling. \"Therefore\", \"suggest\" so'zlari \u2014 oldingi gaplarning mantiqiy natijasini kutadi.",B.PJ)
B.Qz=s(["Since the program began, the number of cars entering downtown each day has fallen by 12 percent.","The bikes in the program are painted bright green.","Many residents say they enjoy cycling on weekends.","The city plans to add more bike stations next year."],t.s)
B.a_q=new A.bw("A student claims that her city's new bike-sharing program has reduced car traffic downtown.","Which finding, if true, would most directly support the student's claim?",B.Qz,"Da'vo \u2014 mashinalar kamaydi. Faqat birinchi variant aynan mashinalar soni haqida.")
B.SJ=s(["The library averaged 650 visitors on Saturday, more than on any of the weekdays listed.","The library averaged 410 visitors on Wednesday and 290 on Friday.","The library averaged 320 visitors on Monday.","The library had fewer visitors on Friday than on Monday."],t.s)
B.ZP=new A.bw("Average daily visitors at a city library:\n\u2022 Monday \u2014 320\n\u2022 Wednesday \u2014 410\n\u2022 Friday \u2014 290\n\u2022 Saturday \u2014 650\n\nThe library manager concluded that the Saturday programs attract more visitors than weekday activities do.","Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to support the manager's conclusion?",B.SJ,"Xulosa shanba va ish kunlarini taqqoslaydi \u2192 shanbani boshqa kunlar bilan solishtirgan variant.")
B.R1=s(['"Library checkouts by students have doubled since the program began."','"The program uses books from several different publishers."','"Some students prefer reading on tablets."','"The program was introduced in September."'],t.s)
B.a_m=new A.bw("Zuhra argues that her school's new reading program has increased students' interest in books.","Which quotation from a teacher's report would best support Zuhra's argument?",B.R1,"Qiziqish oshganini ko'rsatadigan dalil \u2014 kutubxonadan kitob olish ikki barobar ko'paygan.")
B.Tn=s(["between 2015 and 2020, when the share rose by 12 percentage points.","between 2010 and 2015, when the share rose by 12 percentage points.","before 2010, when the share was already 31 percent.","between 2010 and 2020, when the share fell by 19 percentage points."],t.s)
B.a_i=new A.bw("Share of electricity from renewable sources in Country X:\n\u2022 2010 \u2014 12%\n\u2022 2015 \u2014 19%\n\u2022 2020 \u2014 31%\n\nCountry X has rapidly increased its use of renewable energy, with the fastest growth occurring ______","Which choice most effectively uses data from the table to complete the statement?",B.Tn,"Hisoblang: 2010\u21922015: +7; 2015\u21922020: +12. Eng tez o'sish \u2014 2015\u20132020.")
B.RF=s([B.a_q,B.ZP,B.a_m,B.a_i],t.vn)
B.a_w=new A.ed("evidence","Command of Evidence","Dalil bilan isbotlash","\ud83d\udcca","Information and Ideas","Avval aynan qaysi da'vo isbotlanishi kerakligini aniqlang. To'g'ri, lekin da'voga aloqasiz ma'lumot \u2014 xato javob! Jadval/raqamli savollarda: variantdagi raqamlar jadvalga mos bo'lishi VA xulosani qo'llab-quvvatlashi kerak.",B.RF)
B.To=s(["It corrects a common explanation for a feature of old windows.","It introduces the main topic of the text.","It provides an example that supports the idea that glass flows.","It describes how modern glass is manufactured."],t.s)
B.a_6=new A.bw("Many people think of glass as a solid, but its atoms are arranged randomly, like those in a liquid. Unlike a liquid, however, glass does not flow at room temperature in any measurable way. Old windows that are thicker at the bottom were most likely made that way during manufacturing, not as a result of the glass slowly flowing downward over centuries.","Which choice best describes the function of the last sentence in the overall structure of the text?",B.To,"Oxirgi gap \"shisha oqadi\" degan keng tarqalgan tushuntirishni rad etib, to'g'ri sababni beradi.")
B.Qf=s(["To describe how a student project helped reduce plastic waste","To argue that tourists should not visit historic sites","To explain how plastic bottles are recycled","To compare different methods of purifying water"],t.s)
B.ZQ=new A.bw("A group of students in a small town noticed that many visitors left plastic bottles near the town's historic sites. The students designed refill stations where visitors could fill reusable bottles with clean water for free. Within a year, the number of bottles collected near the sites had dropped by nearly half.","Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?",B.Qf,"Matn muammo \u2192 o'quvchilar yechimi \u2192 natijani tasvirlaydi.")
B.T2=s(["By noting that the benefits they describe may depend on the type of workplace","By agreeing that a four-day week increases productivity in every workplace","By arguing that rested employees make more mistakes","By claiming that no company has ever tried a four-day week"],t.s)
B.a_r=new A.bw("Text 1\nSome economists argue that a four-day workweek would increase productivity, because rested employees work more efficiently and make fewer mistakes.\n\nText 2\nA study of companies that tried a four-day week found that the results varied widely. Productivity rose in offices where work could be easily reorganized, but in hospitals and factories, shorter weeks often led to staff shortages.","Based on the texts, how would the author of Text 2 most likely respond to the economists in Text 1?",B.T2,"2-matn: natija ish joyiga bog'liq (ofislarda yaxshi, kasalxona/zavodlarda muammo) \u2192 1-matndagi umumiy da'voni cheklaydi.")
B.Sl=s(["It presents an earlier view, explains why it was revised, and describes current practice.","It lists several earthquakes and their effects on cities.","It argues that skyscrapers should no longer be built.","It compares two cities with different building codes."],t.s)
B.a_s=new A.bw("Engineers once believed that tall buildings had to be extremely rigid to survive earthquakes. Later research showed that rigid structures can crack under strong shaking. Today, many skyscrapers are designed to sway slightly, using flexible materials and special dampers that absorb energy.","Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?",B.Sl,"Tuzilish: avvalgi fikr \u2192 nega o'zgardi \u2192 hozirgi amaliyot.")
B.OW=s([B.a_6,B.ZQ,B.a_r,B.a_s],t.vn)
B.a_E=new A.ed("structure","Text Structure and Purpose","Matn tuzilishi va maqsadi","\ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f","Craft and Structure","Savol \"nima uchun\" deb so'raydi: muallif bu gapni/matnni qaysi maqsadda yozgan? Variantlardagi fe'llarga qarang: describe, argue, explain, contrast, illustrate, challenge. Ikki matnli savolda avval har bir matnning asosiy fikrini alohida aniqlang, keyin ularni solishtiring.",B.OW)
B.Q0=s(["The Ulugh Beg Madrasa was completed in 1420, more than two centuries before the Sher-Dor Madrasa (1636).","The Registan, a public square in Samarkand, is framed by three madrasas.","Both the Ulugh Beg Madrasa and the Sher-Dor Madrasa are located in Samarkand.","The Sher-Dor Madrasa is one of three madrasas that frame the Registan."],t.s)
B.a_l=new A.bw("While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\u2022 The Registan is a public square in Samarkand.\n\u2022 It is framed by three madrasas.\n\u2022 The Ulugh Beg Madrasa was completed in 1420.\n\u2022 The Sher-Dor Madrasa was completed in 1636.\n\nThe student wants to emphasize the difference in when the two madrasas were completed.",u.B,B.Q0,"Maqsad \u2014 qurilish vaqtidagi FARQ. Faqat birinchi variant ikki sanani solishtiradi.")
B.Pm=s(["Mosses, which lack flowers and seeds, reproduce using tiny cells called spores.","Some mosses can survive being completely dried out for years.","Mosses absorb water directly through their leaves.","Mosses are small plants that can survive in many places."],t.s)
B.a_3=new A.bw("While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\u2022 Mosses are small plants that do not have flowers or seeds.\n\u2022 They reproduce using tiny cells called spores.\n\u2022 Mosses can absorb water directly through their leaves.\n\u2022 Some mosses can survive being completely dried out for years.\n\nThe student wants to explain to an audience unfamiliar with mosses how these plants reproduce.",u.B,B.Pm,"Maqsad \u2014 qanday KO'PAYISHINI tushuntirish \u2192 spores haqidagi variant (notanish o'quvchi uchun gulsiz va urug'siz ekani ham aytilgan).")
B.NJ=s(["Paper was invented in China around the 2nd century BCE, many centuries before the printing press was developed in Europe around 1440.","The printing press allowed books to be produced much faster than copying by hand.","Papermaking spread to Samarkand in the 8th century CE.","Both paper and the printing press changed how people shared information."],t.s)
B.a_j=new A.bw("While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:\n\u2022 Paper was invented in China around the 2nd century BCE.\n\u2022 Papermaking spread to Samarkand in the 8th century CE.\n\u2022 The printing press was developed in Europe around 1440.\n\u2022 It allowed books to be produced much faster than copying by hand.\n\nThe student wants to present paper as a much earlier invention than the printing press.",u.B,B.NJ,"Maqsad \u2014 qog'oz ancha OLDIN ixtiro qilinganini ko'rsatish \u2192 ikkala sanani solishtirgan variant.")
B.Rh=s([B.a_l,B.a_3,B.a_j],t.vn)
B.a_D=new A.ed("synthesis","Rhetorical Synthesis","Eslatmalardan foydalanish","\ud83d\udcdd","Expression of Ideas","Bu savollarda hamma variantdagi ma'lumot TO'G'RI bo'ladi! Faqat savolda aytilgan MAQSADGA (taqqoslash, farqni ta'kidlash, notanish o'quvchiga tushuntirish...) aynan mos keladigan variantni tanlang. Avval maqsadni o'qing, keyin eslatmalarni.",B.Rh)
