B.SV=s(['Do you know how many clothes people buy? Today, people buy about 60% more clothes than they did twenty years ago, but they keep them for only half as long. This is called "fast fashion" \u2014 cheap, trendy clothes that we wear a few times and then throw away.',"Fast fashion has a big problem: it is bad for the environment. Making one cotton T-shirt needs about 2,700 litres of water \u2014 that's how much one person drinks in two and a half years! Also, many old clothes end up as rubbish.","So, what can we do? First, buy fewer clothes, but choose good quality ones. Second, try second-hand shops \u2014 you can find unique and fashionable things there. Third, swap clothes with your friends or give them to charity. Finally, if your favourite jeans have a hole, don't throw them away \u2014 repair them!","Remember: being stylish doesn't mean buying new things all the time."],t.s)
